                        at 2026-08-22T09:48:57.221191146Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @errata
                        text "Removed the `cmd.format-descriptions-informal` claim. The node's earlier log called it \"the planned non-runnable meta-rule\", but it was never defined in posix/docs/spec/commands.md, so it stood as a dangling reference that `nplan audit` reported under undefined_refs. Defining it is the wrong repair: the harness only honours a `not-applicable` disposition whose reason quotes an escape phrase verbatim from the rule body (\"unspecified\", \"may\", \"need not\", ...), and this text contains none — it says the section's command formats \"aid the reader in recognizing the command type\" and do \"not formally represent the syntax\", deferring the formal definition to 2.10 Shell Grammar. catalog.py's own guidance covers exactly this case: text about the document rather than about the shell keeps no rule marker and stays as prose. The paragraph remains in commands.md untagged; the stale annotation on parser.rs's parse_command is removed with it. The grammar rules it defers to carry the testable content."
                        after_done true
                    }
                )
