                    {
                        at 2026-08-30T18:15:14.495121013Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Closed. `d07dd1e` landed the feature on 2026-08-24 and the node stayed Doing for six days for the same reason `make-fuzz-runner-containment-aware` did: no `implements`, so the sync has nothing to derive a transition from.\n\nVERIFIED ON `f583633`, not taken from the commit message.\n- `crates/nsh/Cargo.toml` declares `edit = [\"dep:nshedit\", \"dep:nshterm\", \"nsh-platform/edit\"]`, off by default, and `nsh-cli` names it in its dependency on `nsh`.\n- `cargo tree -p nsh -e normal --depth 1` at default features lists `bstr` and `nsh-platform` only: an embedder linking this crate does not get a line editor, which is the whole title.\n- `cargo build -p nsh` (default), `cargo build -p nsh --features edit` and `cargo build -p nsh --example embed` all succeed, so neither half of the `cfg` has rotted.\n\n`e87a5f9` (lock refresh) rode along on the same node and is not part of the claim."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-08-30T18:15:18.536374848Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
            }
        )
        log (
            {
                at 2026-08-15T16:19:16.302610418Z
                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                kind @decision
                text "Operator directive (2026-08-15, verbatim): \"There should be _no unsafe unless absolutely necessary_ and the unsafe should be isolated to its own crate with safe wrappers provided.\" Measured anatomy of the 3271 unsafe ops at 17fc5c6 (documented method, E0133 breakdown): 2411 calls-to-unsafe-fn (74%) — the literal port's `unsafe fn` cascade, which collapses as bodies stop performing unsafe operations and declarations drop; 619 raw-pointer derefs (19%) — concentrated in expand.rs (639 total ops) and parser.rs (313), the C-string word plumbing; 225 mutable-static uses — the 49 remaining statics' read sites (blocked groups + signal exclusion); 16 union-field accesses. Endpoint set by this decision: the syscall/FFI floor (fork/exec/wait/signals/termios/fd ops) — and nothing else — lives in a dedicated crate behind safe wrappers; nsh denies unsafe_code. Two nodes carry the work: owned-words (under owned-data) kills the deref class and lets the unsafe-fn cascade collapse; unsafe-is-a-crate (under shell-as-library) builds the isolation crate. Trend reporting in every node changes meaning: measure against this endpoint, not against \"less than before\"."
            }
        )
    }

