                                    {
                                        at 2026-08-22T15:12:18.408978627Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @note
                                        text "Carried forward from the implementing agent, for the compatibility-profile verification: FUNCNAME, BASH_SOURCE and BASH_LINENO are materialised through `set_entry`, so under `set -a` they would be exported. Bash does not export them. No case in the pinned Oils corpus covers it, so it was flagged rather than fixed blind.\n\nFour cases in `builtin-trap-err` were declined with reasons rather than matched, and the reasons should survive: `trap ERR with redirect` (#18) encodes Bash's own failure to advance $LINENO for a redirect, and matching it would mean suppressing the command-line record on redirect nodes, degrading diagnostics; `trap ERR pipelines without simple commands` (#6) is a Bash double-fire the spec file itself annotates as an anomaly; `set -o errtrace: trap ERR with &` (#12) turns on a distinction between `false &` and `{ ...; } &` for which no principled rule was found, so it was left rather than guessed; `trap ERR with YSH proc` (#19) cannot match because its `case $SH in bash|...)` guard sees a path, which is a harness shape, not shell behaviour."
                                        after_done true
                                    }
