                            {
                                id make-fuzz-runner-containment-aware
                                title "Give fuzz campaigns one containment-aware entry point"
                                kind @test
                                deps (fuzz-the-shell)
                                sealed true
                                log (
                                    {
                                        at 2026-08-25T14:51:07.917246564Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @status
                                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                                    }

                                    {
                                        at 2026-08-30T17:40:51.235873869Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @note
                                        text "Closed. The work landed as `2412863` on 2026-08-25, carrying this node's id, and the claim was never resolved because the node has no `implements` for the sync to derive a transition from -- so it sat Doing for five days with its delivery already in the tree. Verified on `e31a4e3` before closing rather than taken on the commit message's word.\n\nWHAT IS THERE. `fuzz/run.sh` selects one containment layer and says which: `auto` reads `CODEX_SESSION_ID` with a workspace-write permission profile and uses that outer boundary, and otherwise wraps Cargo in `scripts/sandboxed` with `fuzz/` as the one writable bind and a wall clock 120s past the campaign's own. `outer` and `new` force either choice. `--dry-run` prints the selected command instead of running it, which is what makes the choice reviewable rather than inferred, and `--build` stops after `cargo fuzz build` so a replay can execute the binary itself inside the boundary a campaign would have used. `fuzz/sweep.sh` takes the same `--containment` and hands it back to `run.sh`, so there is one entry point and not two.\n\nVERIFIED. `fuzz/run-selftest.sh` exits 0: it exercises the detector three ways -- host with the Codex variables unset reports `containment=new` and names `scripts/sandboxed` and `--chdir`, a managed profile reports `containment=outer` and does *not* nest a second sandbox, and `--containment new` inside a managed profile forces the wrapper back. Both dry runs re-checked by hand here.\n\nWHAT THIS NODE IS NOT. It gave the campaigns one entry point; it did not make anything measure. The containment's own tmpfs over `/tmp` is what made `gate-bash` score a stub shell identically to GNU Bash, and that was `enforce-oracles-cannot-pass-unmeasured`'s to fix."
                                    }

                                    {
                                        at 2026-08-30T17:41:53.049957135Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @status
                                        text "Doing → Done (nplan complete)"
