                                        at 2026-09-02T05:37:05.914425484Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @note
                                        text "A FOURTH CASE FOR THE LIST, measured 2026-09-02 while closing `close-associative-assignment-diagnostics`. `background.test.sh:12` (\\\"Wait for job and PIPESTATUS\\\") flakes the *false-fail* way in `run-oils --group bash-comparison`: it is not in `BASH_COMPARISON_FAILURES.toml`, so it normally passes, and it failed 1 run in 4 here -- once in a full run and once out of three in isolation. Same family as the three already recorded: a process-timing race, not a cost.\n\n`process-sub.test.sh:2` was re-measured at the same time and is unchanged: 1 pass in 3 in isolation, and it flipped in two of four full runs. It had to be put back into the baseline by hand after `--update-baseline` dropped it on the run where it passed, which is the practical cost of the false-pass flake -- the refresh silently records the lucky run and every later run then reports a regression that is not one.\n\nSo a baseline refresh on this group is only as trustworthy as the flakiest case in it, and there are now at least two that can move it. Whatever this node settles on should also say what `--update-baseline` does with a case it knows to be unstable."
                                        after_done true
                                    }
                                )
