                                    {
                                        id register-a-file-nearing-the-density-cap
                                        title "Present the density bill five functions before it is due"
                                        kind @test
                                        sealed true
                                        log (
                                            {
                                                at 2026-09-01T19:44:03.271286084Z
                                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                                kind @note
                                                text "THE CAP IS NOT THE PROBLEM, ITS TIMING IS. `[spec:np:req:dod.function-density]` charges growth rather than level -- probed at `cc887df` -- so a file costs nothing until someone adds to it, and then it costs everything at once. The bill arrives at fifty, during whatever change happened to come next, in a commit about something else. That was five bugfixes in a row in the week of 2026-08-25, and eight files out of about two hundred sitting on exactly fifty is what an attractor looks like rather than a distribution.\n\nWHAT TO BUILD, and it is the same shape as `gate-bash` rather than a second cap. A structural lint kept as a test, beside `oracle_measurement.rs`, `idiomatic_control_flow.rs`, `rust_naming.rs` and `port_provenance.rs`:\n\n  * a file under `crates/` with 45 or more functions must have an entry in a checked-in register, with a reason;\n  * a registered file that has fallen below 45 fails until its entry is removed.\n\nThe second half is what stops it becoming a place to hide, and it is exactly the symmetry `gate-bash` already has -- a registered case that starts passing fails the gate. Registering costs one line and a sentence, and it is the signal to plan the split: five functions of headroom rather than none.\n\nCOUNT IT THE WAY THE GATE DOES, which means inline test functions count. The lint would be lying if it disagreed with the thing it exists to give warning of, and `options.rs` at 28 production functions and 22 tests is precisely the case where the two counts differ.\n\nWATCH IT FAIL BEFORE TRUSTING IT, per this repository's standing bar: point it at a file at 45 with no entry, and at an entry for a file at 30.\n\nDONE WHEN. The register exists with an entry for every file at or above 45 after the splits land, a file crossing 45 without an entry fails the suite, a stale entry fails it too, and both have been seen to."
                                            }

                                            {
                                                at 2026-09-01T23:49:32.93929508Z
                                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                                kind @status
                                                text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
