                                )
                            }

                            {
                                id stop-the-fuzz-budget-paying-for-the-build
                                title "Stop a fuzz run's budget being spent on building it"
                                kind @fix
                                sealed true
                                log (
                                    {
                                        at 2026-09-02T00:37:20.927558951Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @blocker
                                        text "`fuzz/run.sh TARGET SECONDS` gives the sandbox a wall clock of `seconds + 120`, and the `cargo +nightly fuzz` build happens *inside* it. So the build is paid for out of the fuzzing budget, and on a cold cache it can eat most of it.\n\nMeasured 2026-09-02 by the agent decomposing `evaluate_command_in_scope`: `fuzz/run.sh differential 180` needed two rebuilds, 2 minutes 27 seconds of the 300-second wall clock, and the sandbox killed the run at exit 124 with the fuzzer only part-way through its 180 seconds. On a warm build the same command finishes with room to spare.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN THE LOST SECONDS. The truncated run exits 124, which is indistinguishable from the fuzzer having been stopped by its own timeout -- so a cold-cache run looks like a completed short campaign and reports no artifact, when what actually happened is that it barely ran. Every \"no new artifact\" in this week's commits was on a warm cache and is sound, but the failure mode is silent and the next person will not know to check.\n\nIt is the same shape as `[spec:nsh:req:oracle.cannot-measure-is-a-failure]` seen from the clock: a run that could not measure much reports as one that measured and found nothing.\n\nWHAT TO DO. Build before starting the clock -- `fuzz/run.sh --build` already exists for exactly that and `fuzz/sweep.sh` already calls it -- so the wall clock covers only the campaign. Failing that, the runner should say how much of its budget went on the build, so a short campaign is visible as one.\n\nDONE WHEN. A cold-cache `fuzz/run.sh TARGET 180` fuzzes for 180 seconds, or says plainly that it did not."
                                    }

