                            {
                                id stop-selecting-the-locale-per-character
                                title "Stop selecting the thread locale once per character of every match"
                                kind @perf
                                sealed true
                                log (
                                    {
                                        at 2026-09-02T05:31:04.132674211Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @blocker
                                        text "EVERY CHARACTER STEP OF EVERY PATTERN MATCH COSTS TWO `uselocale` CALLS. Found 2026-09-02 while closing `bound-the-cost-of-matching-a-pattern`, by counting rather than by guessing: it is now what that matcher spends most of its time on.\n\n`pattern.rs`'s `character_end` -- reached from `*`, from `?`, from every literal comparison and from every bracket expression -- calls `Locale::multibyte_len`, which is\n\n    with_selected(|| mbrlen(...))    ->    uselocale(ours); mbrlen(one char); uselocale(previous)\n\nso one `mbrlen` of a handful of instructions is wrapped in two thread-locale switches. Counted with a temporary probe on `fuzz/artifacts/matcher/slow-unit-08eff04...` after the alternation fix: 49,540 matcher states and 482,532 `character_end` calls for a 123-byte pattern against a 293-byte subject -- about ten per state, and about 0.07 of the 0.10 seconds the match takes in a release build.\n\nTHE MATCHER IS ONLY WHERE IT WAS MEASURED. `character_end` is the matcher's, but `with_selected` wraps every locale-sensitive primitive in `nsh-platform`: `decode_byte` does it per byte, and `decode_exact`, the collation and the wide-class predicates each do it per call. A shell that decodes its input a byte at a time pays this on every byte it reads.\n\nWHAT IS NOT WRONG. The scoping itself is the point of `[dec:nsh:per-shell-locale]` and `[spec:nsh:req:embedding-safety.process-locale-is-unchanged]`: a `Shell` embedded in a host must not leave the process locale changed, and an `Arc`-owned `locale_t` with a lifetime-bound guard is what makes concurrent `Shell`s independent. That contract is not negotiable and this node does not propose weakening it. What is wrong is the *granularity*: the guard is taken per character where the caller is about to walk a whole string.\n\nWHAT TO DO, and the choice is the work. A scope held across a loop -- `locale.with_selected(|| ...whole match...)` -- restores the contract's guarantee at the same boundary while paying once, but it makes the guard's lifetime cover code that calls back into the shell, which is exactly what the current shape avoids. A decoded-widths table computed once per subject is the other end: `character_end` becomes an index, at the cost of a Vec per match. Measure both before choosing, because the matcher is not the only caller and the two answers suit different callers.\n\nDONE WHEN. The per-character locale switch is gone from the matcher's inner loop, the embedding-safety tests still prove a host's locale is unchanged and that two `Shell`s cannot see each other's, and the saving is a measured number on both trees rather than an argument."
                                    }

                                    {
                                        at 2026-09-02T12:18:13.776036539Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @status
