                                    {
                                        at 2026-09-02T14:02:14.16124926Z
                                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                        kind @note
                                        text "INTERRUPTED MID-FLIGHT 2026-09-02 ~15:0x by an API session limit, not by anything in the work. Six agents were killed in the same second. The node stays Doing and its work is uncommitted in the checkout, not lost:\n\n    crates/nsh-platform/src/locale.rs          +35\n    crates/nsh-platform/src/windows/locale.rs  +11\n    crates/nsh/src/pattern.rs                  +159/-...\n    crates/nsh/tests/locale_isolation.rs       +76 (new coverage)\n\nIts last words were that it was about to file a finding that HEAD did not compile, then take a final end-to-end measurement. **HEAD compiles.** Checked afterwards in a clean detached worktree at `a81455c` with its own `CARGO_TARGET_DIR`: `cargo check --workspace --all-targets` finishes clean. The break it saw was real and transient -- a sibling agent had committed a node without one of its files and repaired it in `a81455c` -- so the finding it wanted to file is already answered and does not need one.\n\nWhat remains, from its own account: the final measurement. The before number is the node's 482,532 `uselocale` calls for a 293-byte subject. Whoever resumes should also confirm the matcher's two work-unit assertions in `pattern.rs` have not moved, since this is meant to be a constant factor and not an algorithmic change.\n\nDo not `git checkout` or `git stash` any of those four paths. The tree is the only copy."
                                    }

