                        )
                    }

                    {
                        id struct.script-module-port
                        title "Port the script module onto the canonical word"
                        kind @refactor
                        constrained_by ([spec:nsh:req:embedding-safety.reading-without-running] [spec:nsh:req:idiom.canonical-tree+1])
                        sealed true
                        log (
                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T17:38:56.822578251Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @blocker
                                text "A 734-LINE PUBLIC MODULE ARRIVED FROM THE REMOTE WRITTEN AGAINST A WORD REPRESENTATION THIS TREE NO LONGER HAS.\n\n`origin/master` carried three commits this checkout had not seen -- `4cc143b`, `9c3f343`, `6d9539c` -- branched from `9788287`, before the word canonicalization. The merge itself is resolved and lives on branch `merge-origin` in the worktree `/data/dash-merge`; six conflicted files were settled and the tree compiles except for this.\n\n`crates/nsh/src/script.rs` is `6d9539c`'s new module, `pub mod script;` on the crate surface: *\"a script as the shell reads it, without running it ... an embedder that composes recursive invocations out of recipe lines needs the shell's reading of a line and not a second grammar of its own.\"* Ronin is the consumer. It is written against:\n\n    WordPart::Literal(BString)      WordPart::Escaped       WordPart::Quote\n    WordPart::Multibyte             QuoteBoundary           Printer::parsed_word\n    Quoting                         WordPart::Command(..)   WordPart::Arithmetic(..)\n\nNone of the first seven exists here, and the last two are struct variants in this tree, not tuple variants. `WordPart` is now `Text { bytes, quoted }` plus struct-shaped `Command` and `Arithmetic`, from `9bad7cb`, `82d4bb9`, `1760d95` and `87e0007` -- the work `[dec:nsh:no-equivalent-forms]` and `[spec:nsh:req:idiom.printable-ast+2]` drove, where one program has one tree and the tree carries the tokens it was read as. `nodes/source.rs` also fails in four places against the same printer API, and their `Node` match does not cover `Node::Group`, which this tree has and theirs did not.\n\nFIFTEEN ERRORS, AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS A CONFLICT MARKER. That is the point: this is not merge resolution, it is porting a module onto a different data model. A careless mapping here is the dangerous kind, because `script.rs` exists precisely to give an embedder *the shell's own reading* of a line -- a plausible-looking translation that quietly loses a quoting distinction produces an embedder that mis-reads recipe text and no test in this repository would notice, since the module is new and nothing here consumes it.\n\nWHAT THE PORT HAS TO PRESERVE. `Literal` vs `Escaped` vs `Quote` vs `Multibyte` were four ways of saying what one `Text { bytes, quoted }` now says together with the token log; `QuoteBoundary` was how the old model marked where a quoted run began and ended. Establish, from the four canonicalization commits and from `word.rs` as it now stands, what carries each of those facts today -- then port each use, and say in the commit message which old distinction maps onto what. Where a distinction genuinely has no counterpart, that is a finding about the canonical form and belongs in a note, not in a guess.\n\nThe module's own tests came with it and are the check that the reading did not move. `Ronin` is the consumer; `nsh` does not use `script` itself, so the tests are all there is.\n\nDo not simply drop `pub mod script;` to make the build green. That would remove a public module a colleague landed hours ago and leave master lying about what it offers."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T17:39:34.261606606Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T18:10:32.608512479Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "THE MAPPING, PART BY PART, AND WHERE THE ONE MISSING DISTINCTION WENT.\n\n`Literal(BString)` -> `Text { bytes, quoted: false }`. `Escaped(u8)` -> `Text { bytes: [byte], quoted: true }`. `Multibyte { bytes, escaped }` -> `Text { bytes, quoted }`, where the decoder has already folded `escaped || inside-quotes` into the one flag -- which is exactly the expression `word_from_parts` was computing by hand (`quoted || *escaped`). `Command(_)` and `Arithmetic(_)` -> the struct variants, and their `quoted` field is now available where the old model had none. `Parameter` keeps its shape and gains `quoted`, so the running `quoted` variable the projection carried across the word is gone: every part answers for itself.\n\n`Quote(QuoteBoundary::Open/Close)` HAS NO COUNTERPART IN THE TREE, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE OF THE PORT'S RISK. The old model bracketed a region; the canonical model records per-run inertness and merges runs of equal inertness, so `'it''s'` and `'its'` are one tree. Its counterpart is the TOKEN RUN, `[dec:nsh:tokens-are-the-truth]`. So `Word::source` is taken from `WordNode::tokens` now -- through `nodes::source::word`, which already prefers a node's run and falls back to `spelled` -- rather than re-spelled from parts. That is strictly better than what it replaced: the embedder is handed the bytes the operator wrote, byte for byte, and `a_words_source_reads_back_as_itself` still gets `'it''s'` back where a structural re-spelling would have said `'its'`. Two words in this module have no run and are spelled from structure instead: the implicit `\"$@\"` of a bare `for`, which the parser builds, and the value half of a `name=value`, which this module cuts.\n\nTHE PROJECTION GAINED A DISTINCTION IT USED TO LOSE. `''` and `\"\"` are an empty inert run in the canonical tree, so they now reach the embedder as `Piece::Literal { bytes: \"\", quoted: true }`. The old model wrote `Quote(Open), Quote(Close)` and `word_from_parts` skipped both, so `a''b` projected to ONE unquoted piece `\"ab\"` and `echo ''` to a word with no pieces at all -- which is what `Word::pieces`' doc said (\"Empty for `''` and `\"\"`\"). That doc is now wrong and is corrected, and `a_quote_that_wrote_nothing_is_a_piece` holds the new reading.\n\n`push_literal`'s merging closure is gone: `push_text` already merges runs of equal inertness when the tree is built, so two adjacent `Text` parts always differ in `quoted` and there is nothing left to join. `word_from_parts(parts, word)` took `parts` and `word` where all three call sites passed `w.parts(), &w`; it is `pieces(&ParsedWord)` and `word_from_node(&WordNode)` now.\n\n`Node::Group` did not exist on the branch this module came from -- `8d14347` added it here, and before that `{ list; }` parsed to `Node::Redirect` around the list. It projects to the list with its redirections on it, which is what the remote's tree produced for the same source and what `redirections_and_negation_and_background_are_kept` already asserted. Nothing is lost by not having a `Command::Group`: `{ a; b; } && c` is `And(Sequence(a,b), c)` and `a; b && c` is `Sequence(a, And(b,c))`, two different shapes, and the braces' whole job -- deciding what a redirection or an `&` attaches to -- is what `Redirected` and `Background` say.\n\nVERIFICATION. The module's 13 tests pass unchanged, with two added. Workspace 80 suites / 912 passed / 0 failed under `LOCPATH=$(tests/build-locales.sh)`; clippy --workspace --all-targets clean; `nsh-lint` 27/27 clean; `gate-bash` PASS (872 eligible, 867 pass, 5 dispositioned, 1 undecided on machine noise); Oils bash-comparison 2735 executed, 2181 pass, 454 fail, baseline matched on all 454. Machine load average 14.8-28.7 across the runs."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T18:14:58.962440378Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @status
                                text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T18:14:58.962440378Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                                kind @note
                                text "claim stolen: Same session, wrong worktree. The claim was taken with project_root /home/brendan/work/dash before the work moved to the merge worktree /data/dash-merge, where branch merge-origin carries the resolved merge. Nothing is being taken from another worker: the claim names this session and this pid."
                            }

                            {
                                at 2026-09-03T18:20:29.9347372Z
                                author "brendan@necessary.nu"
